# AI Civ training situations v1
# Machine row format: correct_output_slot|candidate_output_slots|nonzero_input_slots|target_output_slots|short_description
# Comment blocks explain the game meaning of each slot used by the following machine row.
# situation 0: action settler settlement case: settler stands on grass with A-bit local water source
# Purpose: teach Action engine settlement choices from generic terrain, resources, distance, fresh water, lakes, and A-bit land water sources.
# Object ids are not encoded. Output command record 0 applies to the first unit id stored by ai.js for object record 0.
# Action object fields used here: input[0]=unit type, input[9]=current terrain, input[10]=current resource value, input[11]=nearby resource score, input[12]=fresh-water flag, input[13]=city plot score, input[15]=distance to nearest friendly city.
# A terrain byte with bit 7 set is the A-bit source flag. On land it means a water source in fields, hills, or rocks; in the local window it raises the tile signal above the base terrain value.
# Local 9x9 window slots are input[16..96], scanned row-major from map offset di=-4,dj=-4 to di=+4,dj=+4. Slot input[56] is the visible cue in this example; input[56] is the center tile under this settler.
# Cue meaning: local window center tile is grass plus A-bit land water source.
# Decision meaning: build city because field water source gives food and money immediately.
# Legal output candidates: output[0] = goto; output[1] = wait; output[2] = build city.
# Correct answer: choose output[2] = build city.
# Evaluation rule: after inference, compare only legal candidate outputs; the highest value is the predicted answer.
# Training target: output[2] is set to +0.900000, every other legal candidate output is set to -0.900000.
# input[0] = 0.031250 means Settlers unit type normalized as unitTypeIndex/32.
# input[9] = 0.250000 means current tile terrain type normalized as terrainType/8.
# input[12] = 1.000000 means fresh water is present on or near the settlement candidate.
# input[13] = 0.860000 means city plot score calculated by ai.js from terrain, resources, water sources, and city distance.
# input[56] = 0.370000 means local 9x9 map cue for lake water or A-bit land water source.
# Machine row below repeats the same situation in parser format.
